The Counting Tragedy.

Romeo, who knows where to stop.
Juliet, who counts the letters.

                    Act I: The Count.

                    Scene I: Setting out.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Juliet:
  You are the sum of the sum of a big big big big big big cat and a big big cat and a cat!
Romeo:
  You are the sum of a big big big big big big cat and a cat!

                    Scene II: One letter, then the next.

Romeo:
  Speak your mind!
  You are the sum of yourself and a cat.
  Are you not better than me?
  If so, let us return to scene II.

[Exeunt]
